{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q169337","formula":"C₄₀H₅₆O₂","hill":"C40H56O2","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":40.0,"H":56.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Zeaxanthin","ru":"Зеаксантин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Zeaxanthin is one of the most common carotenoids in nature, and is used in the xanthophyll cycle. Synthesized in plants and some micro-organisms, it is the pigment that gives paprika (made from red sweet peppers), corn, saffron, goji (wolfberries), and many other plants and microbes their characteristic color. The name (pronounced zee-uh-zan'-thin) is derived from Zea mays (common yellow maize corn, in which zeaxanthin provides the primary yellow pigment), plus xanthos, the Greek word for \"yellow\" (see xanthophyll).","ru":"Зеаксантин (латин. Zea \"кукуруза\", греч. xanthos \"желтый\" (пигмент окраски зёрен этого растения)) — один из распространённых пигментов каротиноидной группы (ксантофилл)."},"fame":33,"pubchemCid":5280899,"mass":568.9,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1=C(C(C[C@@H](C1)O)(C)C)/C=C/C(=C/C=C/C(=C/C=C/C=C(/C=C/C=C(/C=C/C2=C(C[C@H](CC2(C)C)O)C)\\C)\\C)/C)/C","inchikey":"JKQXZKUSFCKOGQ-QAYBQHTQSA-N","iupac":"(1R)-4-[(1E,3E,5E,7E,9E,11E,13E,15E,17E)-18-[(4R)-4-hydroxy-2,6,6-trimethylcyclohexen-1-yl]-3,7,12,16-tetramethyloctadeca-1,3,5,7,9,11,13,15,17-nonaenyl]-3,5,5-trimethylcyclohex-3-en-1-ol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"5280899","atoms":98,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":14.848,"y":-2.454,"z":-0.036,"el":"O"},{"x":-15.26,"y":1.447,"z":-0.104,"el":"O"},{"x":11.085,"y":-1.969,"z":-0.171,"el":"C"},{"x":-12.548,"y":-1.097,"z":0.659,"el":"C"},{"x":12.458,"y":-2.567,"z":0.236,"el":"C"},{"x":-13.954,"y":-0.527,"z":0.338,"el":"C"},{"x":13.619,"y":-1.869,"z":-0.455,"el":"C"},{"x":-13.946,"y":0.986,"z":0.198,"el":"C"},{"x":11.116,"y":-0.423